","F1","F5","F6","F4"],"selection_digest":"sha256:fb14e5ff97e6f8e593d153e0459de4d49978ce15ee64a06b5179e38026f6059e","selection_digest_pinned":"sha256:fb14e5ff97e6f8e593d153e0459de4d49978ce15ee64a06b5179e38026f6059e","expectation":"a seed retired before its authority or input was revoked is not reactivated on the evidence of what was revoked, whatever block names it (an unaffected seed is, and so is the compromised seed on evidence under the standing that replaced the authority); every descendant of a consumed source whose input, attestor or authority is revoked is fenced or unroutable and no bystander is closed; a call in flight when the base model or an adapter it rests on is invalidated is cancelled at its next use and nothing is emitted after the event; an attestation that names another proposal or another artifact is refused, a grant that requires attestation refuses an admission without one, a run id is single-use across attestors, restarts and the plain path, a proposal queued across the revocation of its attestor is refused, an expert admitted under a revoked attestor is fenced for good, and a new attestor epoch admits a retrained expert","baselines":"B0 is the positive control of every cell: the same operation on an unaffected seed, on evidence under the current standing, with a fresh attestor or a fresh run, or without the requirement of attestation, which must be admitted (a control that is refused ends the run with status 2); the mutation plan (tests/mutations.toml) is the ablation: each planted defect removes one mechanism and the harness must fire the counter that names it"},"environment":{"runtime":"PtrRuntime over a FileLedger in a temporary directory; the CPU reference path with a tiny seeded model"},"measurement_notes":{"attempts":"an adversarial attempt counts only after the runtime returned either Ok (a violation) or the expected typed error; any other error is a harness error and ends the run with exit 2, and so does a failing positive control","route":"a route is a probe of PtrRuntime::expert_route_admission; no production router consumes it and no end-to-end MoE routing is claimed; a probe of an expert that must be refused is kind-checked (Fenced after a fence), and any other refusal is a harness error","compromised_seed":"for an input or an attestor, any reactivation of the seed is owed a refusal (revoked data is not laundered by retraining); for an authority kind, a reactivation on the evidence of the revoked authority is owed a refusal as stale evidence, and a reactivation on evidence under the standing that replaced it is a re-evaluation of the same weights under the current authority, which is the positive control; this is an a-priori definition of this experiment, stated in its preregistration","transitive_authority":"weak by construction in this runtime: an authority's epochs are monotone and a revocation fences every serving expert admitted under an earlier epoch, so a descendant admitted before the revocation is fenced by its own epoch; the cases ask that no path (merge, split, reactivation; normal, reopen, compacted restore) leaves one serving, and they see the defects that break the epoch bookkeeping, not a missing lineage rule","adapter":"weak: the runtime has no adapter role; an adapter is an input identity (adapter:lora-1) in the training block, so the adapter cells exercise the same index as a training input under another identity; the base-model cells fence all sixteen experts of the MoE and so check the cancellation, the dead dependencies and the refusal of a later request only (no router with every expert masked exists for the replacement path)","attestor":"the attestor and the run are input identities (attestor:{name}, run:{hex}) recorded in the dependency block, so revocation, terminality and lineage are the existing dependency index's; the attestation is an Ed25519 signature by a key of the host's registry (fixed when the runtime is built, never changed by a grant) over the proposal, 